  "term": "dichotic listening",
  "definition": "Dichotic listening is a noninvasive testing method used to examine which brain hemisphere is more dominant for language or speech processing. In psychology and clinical assessment, it is also used as a standard tool for evaluating developmental auditory and language disorders.",
